Drop the unused obs-frontend-api link from mac-virtualcam.

The virtual camera plugin links OBS::frontend-api in CMake but never calls a
single frontend function — `grep -r obs_frontend src/obs-plugin/` returns
nothing. That link is what drags QtCore/QtGui/QtWidgets into the closure,
which our zero-Qt gate (LIVE-REVIEW.md A9) correctly refuses.

Removing it leaves the plugin's behaviour identical: it registers the
`virtualcam_output` and talks to the CoreMediaIO system extension over the
app group. Neither path touches the frontend.

--- a/plugins/mac-virtualcam/src/obs-plugin/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/plugins/mac-virtualcam/src/obs-plugin/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
-target_link_libraries(mac-virtualcam PRIVATE OBS::mach-protocol OBS::libobs OBS::frontend-api)
+target_link_libraries(mac-virtualcam PRIVATE OBS::mach-protocol OBS::libobs)
